         The 24 Armory vehicle/ship weapon+armor Level research buttons' CRequirements are overridden
         here so their Show points at the WoLUHideArmory_* AND nodes (RequirementNodeData.xml), which
         AND the vanilla effective Show node with WoLUNotCountFlag. Human player has the flag → Show
         fails → button hidden; enemy Armories (no flag) → vanilla Show → vanilla button (rule 9).
         The vehicle/ship levels themselves now scale with infantry research via the galaxy sync —
         the static max-grant + grant-to-hide are removed (see LibWoLUnbalanced.galaxy
         libWoLU_DisableArmoryResearch). A same-id <CRequirement> override merges onto the vanilla
         definition; we RE-STATE the Use node explicitly on the Level-2/3 buttons (re-pointing the
         existing vanilla Use node id verbatim) so the inherited Use is unambiguous and only Show is
         changed. Level-1 buttons have no Use in vanilla, so we set only Show. ============================ -->

